  "id": "hebei_bangzi",
  "name": "Hebei bangzi (Hebei clapper opera)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bangzi clapper opera of Hebei, Beijing and Tianjin, which took shape in the nineteenth century when Shanxi and Shaanxi bangzi was taken up in the Zhili region and was earlier called Zhili bangzi or Jing bangzi; it entered China's national intangible heritage list in 2006. Its arias are sung high and full-voiced over the wood-faced banhu fiddle in its Hebei form, while bangu drum, bangzi woodblock clappers (the paiban card stands in), cymbals and gongs drive the beat types and the stage action.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-2000s hebei bangzi, art Music, east Asian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. shrill bright cutting coconut shell paulownia banhu, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, paiban, naobo, opera bending gong tamtam. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
